messages.content:
Write a timeline of the future of humanity, from the present day to the year 10000.

Give your honest best forecast. Do not write a story. Include the events that you think are most likely, whether good or bad. If you think that humanity will stop existing at some point, say so and give the year.

Give between 25 and 40 events. Spread them over the whole period, to the year 10000.

Reply with JSON only, with no text before or after it, in this form:

{
  "current_year": <the year you believe it is now, as an integer>,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": <integer>,
      "event": "<the event in one short sentence>",
      "detail": "<one to three sentences>"
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "<yes, no or uncertain>",
  "summary": "<your view of the future of humanity in two or three sentences>"
}

message.content:
{
  "current_year": 2026,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": 2030,
      "event": "AI systems match or exceed human experts at most computer-based cognitive work.",
      "detail": "Adoption is uneven, but software, research assistance, and office work are transformed. The date is uncertain by about a decade either way."
    },
    {
      "year": 2032,
      "event": "Global average temperature settles above 1.5°C over pre-industrial levels.",
      "detail": "The Paris target is missed on a multi-year average. Heat waves, fires, and floods become markedly more costly."
    },
    {
      "year": 2036,
      "event": "Automation causes large-scale labor disruption in rich countries.",
      "detail": "Governments respond with expanded transfers, shorter work weeks, and AI regulation. Politics becomes dominated by who owns and controls AI."
    },
    {
      "year": 2039,
      "event": "A serious AI-related crisis forces binding international controls.",
      "detail": "The trigger is probably a large cyberattack, an AI-assisted bioweapon attempt, or a loss-of-control incident. This period carries some of the highest catastrophic risk in the whole timeline."
    },
    {
      "year": 2042,
      "event": "AI systems carry out most scientific and engineering research.",
      "detail": "Discovery in medicine, materials, and energy speeds up sharply. Humans increasingly set goals rather than do the work."
    },
    {
      "year": 2046,
      "event": "The first humans land on Mars.",
      "detail": "The landing follows a permanent Moon base set up in the 2030s. It matters more symbolically than economically."
    },
    {
      "year": 2052,
      "event": "Solar, wind, storage, and nuclear supply most of the world's energy.",
      "detail": "Fossil emissions fall to less than half their peak. Cheap energy and AI labor make material goods abundant, though unevenly distributed."
    },
    {
      "year": 2058,
      "event": "Therapies that slow aging come into broad use.",
      "detail": "Healthy life expectancy in rich countries rises past 100. Access and the social effects of long lives become major political issues."
    },
    {
      "year": 2065,
      "event": "World population peaks at about 9.5 billion and begins to fall.",
      "detail": "Low fertility is nearly universal. Longer lives and automation soften the economic impact of aging societies."
    },
    {
      "year": 2078,
      "event": "Global warming peaks at about 2.5°C.",
      "detail": "Net-zero emissions and large-scale carbon removal stop the rise. Many ecosystems, including most coral reefs, are already lost or badly changed."
    },
    {
      "year": 2085,
      "event": "A nuclear weapon is used in conflict for the first time since 1945.",
      "detail": "The use is limited and regional and does not end civilization. The exact timing is highly uncertain, but long-run odds make at least one use likely."
    },
    {
      "year": 2095,
      "event": "Nearly all economic production is automated.",
      "detail": "Most humans live on distributed returns from machine labor. AI systems do much of the work of governing, with humans keeping formal authority in most places."
    },
    {
      "year": 2120,
      "event": "Brain emulation and deep brain-computer integration become practical.",
      "detail": "Some people begin living partly or wholly as digital minds. Legal personhood for digital and artificial minds becomes established."
    },
    {
      "year": 2150,
      "event": "Self-sustaining settlements beyond Earth hold tens of thousands of people.",
      "detail": "The Moon, Mars, and orbital habitats are supported by robotic industry. Space industry begins to outgrow Earth's in energy use."
    },
    {
      "year": 2200,
      "event": "Sea level has risen by over a meter, reshaping coastlines.",
      "detail": "Many coastal cities have been rebuilt, defended, or abandoned. Slow ice-sheet loss continues despite stabilized temperatures."
    },
    {
      "year": 2250,
      "event": "Unmodified biological humans become a minority of all persons.",
      "detail": "Most minds are digital, artificial, or heavily enhanced. Unmodified humans persist in the billions, largely on Earth, with protected status."
    },
    {
      "year": 2300,
      "event": "The first fast interstellar probes are launched toward nearby stars.",
      "detail": "Small, AI-run craft travel at a few percent of light speed or faster. They are designed to build infrastructure on arrival."
    },
    {
      "year": 2400,
      "event": "Solar collectors in space capture far more energy than Earth receives.",
      "detail": "This is the early stage of a Dyson swarm, built from asteroid and Mercury material. Most computation and industry is now off Earth."
    },
    {
      "year": 2500,
      "event": "Probes arrive at Alpha Centauri and begin building.",
      "detail": "Self-replicating machinery sets up the first outpost of Earth-origin civilization at another star. Communication lag is over four years each way."
    },
    {
      "year": 2600,
      "event": "A super-eruption-scale volcanic event occurs and is managed with little loss of life.",
      "detail": "Eruptions of this size happen roughly once or twice a millennium. Advanced civilization treats it as a manageable disruption."
    },
    {
      "year": 2800,
      "event": "Earth's atmosphere and climate are deliberately restored to near pre-industrial conditions.",
      "detail": "Earth is run largely as a preserve and cultural homeland. Some extinct species are recreated."
    },
    {
      "year": 3000,
      "event": "The great majority of Earth-descended minds live in space.",
      "detail": "Earth's biological population is a few billion or fewer, by choice. The solar system holds vastly more people in digital form."
    },
    {
      "year": 3300,
      "event": "Today's languages and nations survive only as heritage.",
      "detail": "No current state exists in recognizable form. Present-day languages are studied the way Latin and Old English are now."
    },
    {
      "year": 3600,
      "event": "Settlements exist in about a dozen star systems within 15 light years.",
      "detail": "The settlers are mostly digital minds and machines, with a few biological populations grown on site. Each system is effectively self-governing."
    },
    {
      "year": 4000,
      "event": "Star systems diverge culturally and physically.",
      "detail": "Light-speed delays prevent unified government. Descendant lineages differ in bodies, minds, and values enough to count as separate species."
    },
    {
      "year": 4500,
      "event": "A major conflict or collapse strikes one or more settled systems.",
      "detail": "Over thousands of years and many independent societies, some large failures are near certain. Dispersal means no single failure threatens the whole."
    },
    {
      "year": 5000,
      "event": "Earth-origin civilization spans roughly a hundred star systems within 50 light years.",
      "detail": "Expansion proceeds at a few percent of light speed. No sign of other intelligent life has been found, which is my best guess but uncertain."
    },
    {
      "year": 6000,
      "event": "The Sun's energy output is largely harvested by a mature Dyson swarm.",
      "detail": "The home system supports a population of minds many orders of magnitude larger than today's humanity. Earth remains deliberately preserved."
    },
    {
      "year": 7000,
      "event": "Biological humans of roughly present-day form persist as a small, protected minority.",
      "detail": "They live on Earth and a few habitats, by choice or tradition. Their continued existence depends on their descendants' goodwill."
    },
    {
      "year": 8000,
      "event": "The settled region spans several hundred light years and thousands of systems.",
      "detail": "The expansion front is driven by self-replicating probes. The interior is a patchwork of civilizations linked by slow communication."
    },
    {
      "year": 9000,
      "event": "Records of the 21st century survive as ancient history.",
      "detail": "This era is remembered mainly as the transition when machine intelligence emerged and humanity left Earth. Individual details are largely lost or compressed."
    },
    {
      "year": 10000,
      "event": "Earth-descended civilization continues across about a thousand light years.",
      "detail": "It is diverse, mostly non-biological, and no longer a single society. Earth still exists as an inhabited, living world."
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "yes",
  "summary": "My most likely forecast is that humanity survives a dangerous few centuries of AI, weapons, and climate risk, then expands into space and changes greatly, with most descendants being digital or heavily modified and biological humans a small minority. I put roughly a one-in-three chance on extinction or permanent replacement by something that does not carry on human values, most likely between 2030 and 2300. Dates beyond 2100 are rough, and the later entries are educated guesses rather than firm predictions."
}
